// Stand-in for the now-UNCONDITIONAL str.cla manifest entry (Plan 5b Task
// 8) in this fake runtime-module directory (Task 4's inclusion-machinery
// test, internal/lowlevel/rtinc_test.go). Deliberately empty: this
// directory exercises expand's declare-before-use splicing machinery, not
// str.cla's real content -- the real module lives at runtime/clarus/
// str.cla. main.cla now always adds "str.cla" to neededMods regardless of
// usage flags, so --rtdir testdata/rtinc/rt needs SOME file by that name
// (an empty/decl-less file pushes main.cla's own "-1 head" empty-file
// sentinel, already handled) or TestRtInc's IncludesRuntimeModule/
// NoInclusionWithoutUsage subtests fail with "runtime module str.cla not
// found" before ever reaching the assertions they actually care about.
